.TH FLATPAK-BATCH-INSTALLER 1 "October 2026" "flatpak-batch-installer @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
flatpak-batch-installer \- select many Flathub apps and install them at once
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B flatpak-batch-installer
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B flatpak-batch-installer
loads the Flathub application catalog, lets you search it, tick multiple
applications in a graphical table, and installs all selected apps in a
single Flatpak operation. With no options it opens the GUI; with options
it works headless from the terminal.
.PP
Everything the tool does is a standard
.BR flatpak (1)
command, always shown before it runs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print catalog apps, one per line (ID, name, summary).
.TP
.BI "\-\-search " TEXT
Filter text for \fB\-\-list\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-installed
Print installed app IDs for the chosen scope.
.TP
.BI "\-\-install " APP_ID...
Install the given app IDs in one Flatpak call.
.TP
.BI "\-\-scope " user|system
Flatpak installation scope (default: \fBuser\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-help\-guide
Print the in-app usage guide and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command help and exit.
.SH GUI KEYS
F1 help, F5 reload, Ctrl+F filter, Ctrl+S / Ctrl+O save / load selection,
Ctrl+Enter install, Ctrl+A tick page, Space tick rows, Esc clear filter.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR flatpak-install (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by the Flatpak Batch Installer contributors.
.br
Bugs: https://github.com/ell-shad/flatpak-batch-installer/issues
